Hi, (please keep me on CC)=0A=0A in order to improve IO behavior on my bran=
d new DELL Presision M4500 notebook, I have decided to try out a newer kern=
el compared to the 2.6.18-xxx CentOS one.=0A=0A Installing 2.6.35.4 went pr=
etty well and besides small problems with two =0Aexternal/proprietary modul=
es (my fault, I know ...) I only see two issues:=0A=0Aa) accessing the HW c=
lock does not work=0A=0A[root@lbwjxqm1 ~]# hwclock=0ACannot access the Hard=
ware Clock via any known method.=0AUse the --debug option to see the detail=
s of our search for an access method.=0A[root@lbwjxqm1 ~]# hwclock --debug=
=0Ahwclock from util-linux-2.13-pre7=0Ahwclock: Open of /dev/rtc failed, er=
